{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_17cfd494612e019f235ee8c26ac4bb7241215c750aa4c0e5511885bf0e256f17","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_eb78977db114ea45b946d61539c49647ffab519288f64f5bee0c090e11f39297"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"Ollama is supported as an alternative to an Anthropic subscription via ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=ollama plus ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL pointing at the Ollama endpoint.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2b208af703c1309fb14678ddb1b7ef43ee00b56bbb84f4603add6d94b813f4e8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1ce86628d77011e438b1d024425f45ebcf19b89813b4385c5523e6d8f2fc4c8c","slc_5c7bb472f7982d2aa0c8cca431cfa00b462adbdd7ba1f768e613e2a3cd5d832d","slc_b97af7ad781902e897961caaae85c839b244d71d6e2db71482a4ec077a87c395"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"Environment variables are documented as all optional, covering timezone (TZ), UID/GID remapping (PUID/PGID), Node heap size, SMB polling flags, Apprise notification URLs (Discord, Telegram, Slack, email, etc.), and AI provider API keys.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4350ee935bbe2b417106246efadca148d48c44ccbad14fa9ae7377c5a1dd2b92","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_09dd1c819c66e651d678ab21965b90a38de6292873d1cc23cbab5a60c4d42de4","slc_9bedcb6415ffc14b55dc78c2d6b13b407c2f3cf4ca01eb692ad6369c63db9936","slc_daa8cf01f85980df8d21c400808c6391b637188a420048bad3db7d180ec0f1af"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"Desloppify ships as a passive CLI in both images; it performs no scans or workspace edits unless invoked, and optional global skill setup at container start is controlled by HOLYCLAUDE_DESLOPPIFY_SETUP with values like off, claude, codex, gemini, all, or opencode (full image only).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_59ddcfbeb481916d3b6946b5013ee2b96a275f36e1180002e410367686d3a887","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1235fdc138b201fefda7f5f7079dd431cd0f4898f4257fea8bc34892393814df","slc_8ee720b7f18b1f96f9a3af2647ae53bc03f105edc2be0465d2eb742d40c03a08","slc_c31860f5017ee4eca092d704d6601d7a7c4b635c888b8ca4dd73a2c93fb90780","slc_f28c4ceeeff7a910ff3ca3ceb49fcea34d46adc834ff9ab7532515d278edb972"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"Authentication is done through the CloudCLI web UI: Claude Max/Pro users sign in via OAuth and API-key users paste their key; the container relays no credentials, with tools reading them from container files, bind mounts, or environment variables.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5e6130c76f958b181253973a2144dcad524b001dad5c6d3229d075ef86daa7fb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5293dab535255490ec749f0b4114a17f4b4b288ecf4c0533b956fbea5a2aced7","slc_ada7eac48cce8d0de039cadfbf3c4c45b0789c6d8826f19d70fd45443c205627","slc_d95e3dec789b7ce264956a921a3ffa9b7cd52aa1165fec02cb9dc43145db20a1"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"The compose templates set shm_size 2g because Chromium heavily uses /dev/shm and Docker's 64MB default causes tab crashes, and grant SYS_ADMIN, SYS_PTRACE, and seccomp=unconfined as the retained browser profile, with hardening described as a separate change.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_834c894ec4750c146a70875c9668e9f65d391410dc5fa087059421ce06d2e324","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0ca0d2ecb15b58e72b32e66ee068541c7b5f03ffde757724dfd44c8767f49eaa","slc_5870c7b47c0dde4cd2d46f7a4ccdd1b04687e5e9b530c385d32ecd438e64dcc4"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"OpenAI API keys cannot authenticate Claude Code; they work with the bundled Codex CLI instead, and ChatGPT Plus/Pro subscribers authenticate Codex via codex login --device-auth, optionally exposing port 1455 for the browser callback flow.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_996a0de973fd74e5a31437dedd19160c5089ba00a1795d1bfc807932414257ac","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0f144a46b7c5ee399b586b864f344e1e6bf80836ed8e3b36023f731de00e1571","slc_5293dab535255490ec749f0b4114a17f4b4b288ecf4c0533b956fbea5a2aced7","slc_86f711f30a53e222a2c90b8dcae5bca946b8680009ede7b4ee9275237419966d","slc_d54d470e27cdf34c88e3ed95e7aff541aefe62d1aa4cd52fc1d526032e2c7c19","slc_de4de2d297e2e89e75bb7fc2d7769c47f4d1d66a3fd177f356a0badbb0eb84da"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"Persistence is via bind mounts: ./data/claude maps to /home/claude/.claude (holding settings, credentials, and Claude's memory) and ./workspace maps to /workspace; on every boot Git/gh config is linked into the .claude mount, and bootstrap.sh copies defaults only on first boot, marking it with .holyclaude-bootstrapped.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_adb2dd625e4f4f78c5bf22b20786152810090a2ae97a76e0d5a48d73361732f5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d543f2a24e7979663700750a779a3a7281d8c02496ca6d94d570116921572d2","slc_6fbcd53de5eaeaede8314344235e19de729bec53d4fc1bb36bfa8cd703a19ea3"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"The image bundles Chromium with Xvfb and Playwright for headless browser screenshots and testing, plus database clients (psql, redis-cli, sqlite3, MariaDB-based mysql) and GitHub CLI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ba4eb6720683133398e9d74a0b7448d09ffb76f5cf15343d24c31930336d01d4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_31c8f8c0014bdf1c19f8662518f6b674e6372342042e4e34493c7b970e190aac","slc_6a1f5c419efa9d704c7e11482e545e2c75473ef230e7579401cd664ab1e4cb3b","slc_917d05fb65a2607a402118308a92cbca03925427a9e6e21f490565e5f7d494ce","slc_d56520092bd8fa07fe6378af8d6b4e8abbfceabe99f6d179160ed4839a8e608f","slc_f3b75bbc45e00eb3d89f31164bd35bab819eab29ae7fffddacc6a9ee41bc38e1"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"The full image ships eight AI CLIs — Claude Code, Gemini, Codex, Cursor, TaskMaster, Junie, OpenCode, and Pi — while the slim image ships the five core ones (Claude Code, Gemini, Codex, Cursor, TaskMaster), with slim installing missing tools on demand.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c0254316595719bf4d7309a6333c3b2ad47fd4d18192cf89ce16862df5350254","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_09c09b6e81c61aec598fc63d5909fc0ed6be18cce5f1cd706d11c284d102875d","slc_1d543f2a24e7979663700750a779a3a7281d8c02496ca6d94d570116921572d2","slc_26dfd12f1875bac963dea407421b1a1be09104d394400e6f2fcc77323a8a6eef"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"The container runs the official Anthropic Claude Code CLI (not a wrapper or proxy), served through a CloudCLI web UI on port 3001, with s6-overlay as PID 1 supervising Xvfb on :99 and optional sshd.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d15804f92f7e1ee1bba4295ee9384bad14f7e4e4b819f430e2e1cc1a7d398bc5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_28362a3379c1f1fac8dfb3cce886fe79bcaabd3f40fd61e10ea0e3beea515f03","slc_398681a0b6237bce22f010a6de951fcb98137485c44e61c58d0fa79dc5b4988a","slc_901544948f7d26b42ab895d05183efe8248d2d3ab84f4ee53174d75426296f48","slc_b393bf13b1fc6d3dd189c9f8856f0e6655c09e574b6ec2cb3128961b0167a3bd","slc_e02f1fcdd4147c3a62f004dcb9d72a73430e073fb8775eaf45235238e40bee44"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"The quick-start workflow is: create a docker-compose.yaml from a provided template, run docker compose up -d, then open http://localhost:3001 and create a CloudCLI account; no .env file is required.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e3f3cc373802532e8d253e4bc5de229305fe7150ec357f3d2b6b34787a9dcb4d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5293dab535255490ec749f0b4114a17f4b4b288ecf4c0533b956fbea5a2aced7","slc_57ddc1c79e8994ef4ecaf4934ea7b4a3c9018e44c82224c83b7280bcd2b7fd5e","slc_ada7eac48cce8d0de039cadfbf3c4c45b0789c6d8826f19d70fd45443c205627"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"The web UI port is bound to 127.0.0.1 by default, and users needing remote access are directed to Tailscale or Cloudflare Tunnel rather than port forwarding.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_efbd9e32c74522b076cb6d5e75c71d85b485f5c9fc709f8e340aa7664e2cd9e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4eee7b533e34b78ba229065b2d50669c030c0399dae4af3b4c7313ad91e06478"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"Repository development practice: release-sensitive facts are published in contracts/product-facts.json, and the release workflow checks that contract against the Dockerfile and Compose files before building images.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f84a68605642efca20febf07e64953adaa33b80fd95f29ace6b5e951a4219855","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"coderluii/holyclaude@651c48fc01a9 snapshot ec0da588070ffb78","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_140813cace7cfbdfbdcae4481e51ee266177aaf3ea9bacbd9cbfe4ce45706842","slc_1a6c6102ddbb1d76a1d35cccc6740203b7465ec995a82bcff6efbb27ce43a58b"],"source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"text":"Two image variants are published on Docker Hub: latest (full, everything pre-installed) and slim (core tools only, with Claude installing extras on demand), plus pinned X.Y.Z and X.Y.Z-slim tags for production stability.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
